<% content_for :title, "Malagueña" %>

<div class="manifesto">
  <p class="eyebrow">The idea</p>
  <h1>Just play.</h1>

  <p class="manifesto-lead">
    Every tuner app and every tab site wants something from you before you
    play a note — an account, a subscription, an ad break, one more popup.
    This one wants nothing.
  </p>

  <p>
    Malagueña is four small tools that stay out of the way: a library of
    tab music, a tuner that listens, a metronome that doesn't drift, and
    daily practice routines that run themselves. No sign-ups, no upsells,
    nothing between you and the strings.
  </p>

  <p class="manifesto-story">
    It takes its name from the piece that made me pick the guitar back up.
  </p>

  <div class="toolbar manifesto-actions">
    <%= link_to "Tune up", tuner_path, class: "btn" %>
    <%= link_to "Start a routine", routines_path, class: "btn btn-ghost" %>
  </div>
</div>
